// The demo world's second pass, `demo-gb-v2 [illustrative]` (docs/demo/WORLD-V2.md): 93 historic counties
// of the United Kingdom, each its own node running GOODS-CHAIN's stage v2a.1 under rule A:
// land grows fodder, a maker breeds horses, a capacity desk holds the herd and hires out
// horse-days, and the good desk buys horse-days and labour (P2.2a's roles, HORSES-RULES).
//
// Generated: do not edit. `rustyecon worldgen worlds/demo-gb --stage v2a1 --out
// tapes/demo-gb-v2.ron` writes it from worlds/demo-gb/*.csv (stage-v2a1.csv and
// machine_types.csv among them) and the atlas data/atlas/gb.atlas.ron (ec2ee4100a483601),
// and the test `demo_v2_tape_is_its_compilers_output` checks this file against the compiler.
//
// Illustrative: every entry's basis is Assumed("illustrative demo v2a.1, 2026-09-30: ...") and the name
// carries [illustrative], so nothing from this tape may be scored or cited (R4, R5).
//
// The horse (machine_types.csv): delta = 0.08 a year (0.0016022075724025087 a tick), kappa = 52.0 horse-days a
// head a year (1.0 a tick), omega = 0.85, J_b = 1 tick. Each county's flow machine (a, lam, b)
// becomes fodder's land omega*b and a head's own horse-days a*kappa/delta, labour
// lam*kappa/delta and pasture (1 - omega)*b*kappa/delta, per tick (crates/worldgen/src/chain.rs).
//
// Genesis puts every county at its own oracle point (WORLD-V2 §5): unit 1g's ChainEconomy
// (crates/oracle; the horse's hours at J = 2, decision 232) at the county's per-tick instance,
// under the horses genesis rule (HORSES-SPEC §5.3), every price and coin divided by p/r so
// that the good costs 1 coin. No agent reads the oracle at run time (R13).
//
// The history is v1's, mapped (WORLD-V2 §3): 33332 dated SetParam steps on 1706 dates. A b
// step sets fodder.land and horse.land together, lam horse.labour, a horse.own_hours, and the
// rest themselves; each copies a schedule param county.<c>.<param>.<YYYY-MM> whose basis names
// the ramps of worlds/demo-gb/history.csv that moved it.
Tape(
    schema: 1,
    header: (
        name: "demo-gb-v2 [illustrative]",
        start: "1750-01-01",
        ticks_per_year: 52,
        market: (rule: Imbalance, one_sided: Saturate, ema_time_constant: "price.ema_tc"),
        ledger: (rel_flow: "ledger.rel_flow", rel_stock: "ledger.rel_stock"),
    ),
    params: [
        // The ledger's tolerances and the dials, shared by every county (stage-v2a1.csv).
        (key: "ledger.rel_flow", value: 1e-12, unit: Dimensionless, basis: Assumed("illustrative demo v2a.1, 2026-09-30: July REL_FLOW, as the gate world and v1")),
        (key: "ledger.rel_stock", value: 1e-11, unit: Dimensionless, basis: Assumed("illustrative demo v2a.1, 2026-09-30: July REL_STOCK, as the gate world and v1")),
        (key: "rate.labour", value: 5.2, unit: RatePerYear, basis: Assumed("illustrative demo v2a.1, 2026-09-30: C2g (D-G13), P2.2a's registered dials (HORSES-SPEC 5): the wage is the fastest price")),
        (key: "rate.land", value: 0.1625, unit: RatePerYear, basis: Assumed("illustrative demo v2a.1, 2026-09-30: C2g: land's rate C2's divided by 8 (HORSES-SPEC 5)")),
        (key: "rate.fodder", value: 5.2, unit: RatePerYear, basis: Assumed("illustrative demo v2a.1, 2026-09-30: C2g: fodder at C2L's type rate (HORSES-SPEC 5.1; decision 226)")),
        (key: "rate.horse", value: 5.2, unit: RatePerYear, basis: Assumed("illustrative demo v2a.1, 2026-09-30: C2g: the machine market's rate (HORSES-SPEC 5)")),
        (key: "rate.traction", value: 5.2, unit: RatePerYear, basis: Assumed("illustrative demo v2a.1, 2026-09-30: C2g: the hour market's rate (HORSES-SPEC 5)")),
